<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 13 March, from 1519 to 1996.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1519 CE <span class="tih-ago">507 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hernán Cortés lands on the Mexican coast</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cortés's expedition of about 500 men reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabasco">Tabasco</a> coast. Within two and a half years, with Indigenous allies, he overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1639 CE <span class="tih-ago">387 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New College in Massachusetts is named after John Harvard</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The college at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambridge">Cambridge</a> took the name of John Harvard, a young minister who left it his library and half his estate. Founded in 1636, Harvard is the oldest university in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1781 CE <span class="tih-ago">245 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Herschel discovers Uranus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">From his garden in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bath">Bath</a>, Herschel spotted an object he first took for a comet. It proved to be a new planet, the first discovered with a telescope, doubling the known size of the solar system.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1881 CE <span class="tih-ago">145 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tsar Alexander II assassinated in St Petersburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Members of the revolutionary group People's Will threw bombs at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a>'s carriage. Alexander, who had freed the serfs, died within hours, and his son's reign brought harsh reaction.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1940 CE <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Winter War ends as the Moscow Peace Treaty takes effect</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> ceded about a tenth of its territory, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a>, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. Its stubborn defence had cost the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> heavily and preserved Finnish independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1996 CE <span class="tih-ago">30 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gunman kills 16 children and their teacher at Dunblane</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thomas Hamilton opened fire in the gym of Dunblane Primary School in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> before killing himself. Public campaigning led to a near-total ban on private handgun ownership in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li></ol>
